        {
          "id": "title",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "#1 · Peau noire, masques blancs, chapter I (French text, PDF pp.36–56)",
          "title": "Speaking opens access and installs a measure",
          "italic": "The scene demonstrates the double movement: real acquisition, and the alienation that can accompany it — the mask is socially effective because it can do something.",
          "body": "",
          "x": 0.04,
          "y": 0.05,
          "width": 560,
          "size": 30,
          "align": "left"
        },
        {
          "id": "body",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "",
          "title": "",
          "italic": "",
          "body": "The Antillean speaker enters a language whose social authority precedes his arrival. Linguistic skill opens real capacities of participation — treating it as an empty disguise would erase them. But the authority attached to the skill becomes a rule for self-evaluation: he hears himself through the standard by which the dominant world hears him, and an inward criterion can be turned on others whose speech does not satisfy it.",
          "x": 0.04,
          "y": 0.55,
          "width": 620,
          "size": 14,
          "align": "left",
          "w": 620
        },
